The user wants to add sounds. We need to implement sound loading and playback for jump and game over presumably. Need audio files; we don't have any assets. We could generate simple beep using Web Audio API without external files. Simpler: use AudioContext to play a short oscillator tone for jump, and another for game over.

Add sound functions: createAudioContext, playJumpSound, playGameOverSound.

Add event listener for jump to play sound. Also in game over after cancelAnimationFrame display message, play sound.

We need to modify game.js accordingly.

Let's edit: add sound init at top after canvas.

Add code:

const AudioContext = window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext;
const audioCtx = new AudioContext();

function playTone(freq, duration) { const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator(); const gain = audioCtx.createGain(); osc.frequency.value = freq; osc.connect(gain).connect(audioCtx.destination); gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.1, audioCtx.currentTime); osc.start(); osc.stop(audioCtx.currentTime + duration); }

function playJumpSound(){ playTone(400, 0.1); }

function playGameOverSound(){ playTone(100, 0.3); }

In keydown for space, after setting vy, call playJumpSound.

In game over block, after drawing text, call playGameOverSound.

Also ensure audio context resume on user interaction (iOS). Could call audioCtx.resume() on keydown if state suspended.

Implement.

